  {
    "chapter": 13,
    "title": "Chapter 13: Cross-Cutting Application of Physics",
    "definitionTitle": "Definition",
    "definition": "Agricultural physics is the application of physics principles and methods to agricultural systems, including soil science, plant physiology, and agricultural engineering.",
    "conceptTitle": "Key Concept",
    "concept": "The energy balance in soils is governed by the first law of thermodynamics: \\(Q = mc\\Delta T\\) where: \\(Q\\) is the heat energy transferred \\(m\\) is the mass of soil \\(c\\) is the specific heat capacity of soil \\(\\Delta T\\) is the temperature change",
    "exampleTitle": "Example",
    "example": "Calculate the heat required to raise the temperature of 1 hectare of soil (to 15 cm depth) by 5°C. Assume soil density of 1.3 g/cm³ and specific heat capacity of 0.8 J/g°C.",
    "exampleSolution": "First, calculate the mass of soil: \\(\\text{Area} = 1\\,\\text{hectare} = 10{,}000\\,\\text{m}^2 = 10^8\\,\\text{cm}^2\\) \\(\\text{Volume} = \\text{Area} \\times \\text{depth} = 10^8\\,\\text{cm}^2 \\times 15\\,\\text{cm} = 1.5 \\times 10^9\\,\\text{cm}^3\\) \\(\\text{Mass} = \\text{Density} \\times \\text{Volume} = 1.3\\,\\text{g/cm}^3 \\times 1.5 \\times 10^9\\,\\text{cm}^3 = 1.95 \\times 10^9\\,\\text{g}\\) Now calculate the heat required: \\(Q = mc\\Delta T = (1.95 \\times 10^9\\,\\text{g}) \\times (0.8\\,\\text{J\\,g}^{-1}\\,^{\\circ}\\text{C}^{-1}) \\times (5\\,^{\\circ}\\text{C}) = 7.8 \\times 10^9\\,\\text{J}\\)",
    "figure": "<svg width=\"560\" height=\"330\" viewBox=\"0 0 560 330\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n            <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"560\" height=\"330\" fill=\"#f7fbff\"/>\n            <rect x=\"0\" y=\"230\" width=\"560\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#d9c2a3\"/>\n            <line x1=\"0\" y1=\"230\" x2=\"560\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\"/>\n            <circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"60\" r=\"26\" fill=\"#ffd633\" stroke=\"#e6b800\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n            <line x1=\"70\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"6\" stroke=\"#e6b800\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#guide-13-f133gold)\"/>\n            <line x1=\"70\" y1=\"102\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"114\" stroke=\"#e6b800\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#guide-13-f133gold)\"/>\n            <line x1=\"28\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"16\" y2=\"60\" stroke=\"#e6b800\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#guide-13-f133gold)\"/>\n            <line x1=\"112\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"124\" y2=\"60\" stroke=\"#e6b800\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#guide-13-f133gold)\"/>\n            <line x1=\"40\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"32\" y2=\"22\" stroke=\"#e6b800\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#guide-13-f133gold)\"/>\n            <line x1=\"100\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"108\" y2=\"98\" stroke=\"#e6b800\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#guide-13-f133gold)\"/>\n            <line x1=\"100\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"108\" y2=\"22\" stroke=\"#e6b800\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#guide-13-f133gold)\"/>\n            <line x1=\"40\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"32\" y2=\"98\" stroke=\"#e6b800\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#guide-13-f133gold)\"/>\n            <text x=\"70\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#666666\">sun</text>\n            <line x1=\"150\" y1=\"95\" x2=\"255\" y2=\"205\" stroke=\"#cc0000\" stroke-width=\"3\" marker-end=\"url(#guide-13-f131red)\"/>\n            <text x=\"150\" y=\"82\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#cc0000\">Rn net radiation</text>\n            <line x1=\"325\" y1=\"205\" x2=\"325\" y2=\"95\" stroke=\"#0066cc\" stroke-width=\"3\" marker-end=\"url(#guide-13-f131blue)\"/>\n            <text x=\"290\" y=\"85\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#0066cc\">H sensible heat</text>\n            <line x1=\"400\" y1=\"205\" x2=\"430\" y2=\"95\" stroke=\"#009966\" stroke-width=\"3\" marker-end=\"url(#guide-13-f131green)\"/>\n            <text x=\"445\" y=\"85\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#009966\">LE latent heat</text>\n            <line x1=\"480\" y1=\"245\" x2=\"480\" y2=\"315\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" marker-end=\"url(#guide-13-f131brown)\"/>\n            <text x=\"370\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\">G soil heat</text>\n            <text x=\"20\" y=\"215\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#666666\">atmosphere</text>\n            <text x=\"20\" y=\"320\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#5c3d1f\">soil</text>\n            <defs>\n                <marker id=\"guide-13-f131red\" markerWidth=\"10\" markerHeight=\"7\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"3.5\" orient=\"auto\">\n                    <polygon points=\"0 0, 10 3.5, 0 7\" fill=\"#cc0000\"/>\n                </marker>\n                <marker id=\"guide-13-f131blue\" markerWidth=\"10\" markerHeight=\"7\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"3.5\" orient=\"auto\">\n                    <polygon points=\"0 0, 10 3.5, 0 7\" fill=\"#0066cc\"/>\n                </marker>\n                <marker id=\"guide-13-f131green\" markerWidth=\"10\" markerHeight=\"7\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"3.5\" orient=\"auto\">\n                    <polygon points=\"0 0, 10 3.5, 0 7\" fill=\"#009966\"/>\n                </marker>\n                <marker id=\"guide-13-f131brown\" markerWidth=\"10\" markerHeight=\"7\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"3.5\" orient=\"auto\">\n                    <polygon points=\"0 0, 10 3.5, 0 7\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n                </marker>\n            </defs>\n        </svg>",
    "figureCaption": "Figure 13.1: Surface energy balance of a soil"
  }
